# COMPACTNESS_RATIO
# Feature description: Ratio of COMPACTNESS to PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO.
# Usefulness: Captures the relationship between compactness and axis proportions. Vehicles like OPEL or SAAB may exhibit higher compactness relative to their aspect ratio, while larger vehicles like BUS or VAN might demonstrate lower compactness ratios. This enhances the ability to differentiate between vehicle types based on shape and proportions.
df['COMPACTNESS_RATIO'] = df['COMPACTNESS'] / (df['PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO'] + 1e-5)
end

python
# SKEWNESS_RATIO
# Feature description: Ratio of SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS to SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS.
# Usefulness: Reflects the comparative asymmetry between the minor and major axes. Smaller vehicles might have balanced skewness, whereas larger vehicles such as VAN or BUS might show pronounced asymmetry. This ratio provides insight into shape asymmetry.
df['SKEWNESS_RATIO'] = df['SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MINOR_AXIS'] / (df['SKEWNESS_ABOUT_MAJOR_AXIS'] + 1e-5)
end

python
# NORMALIZED_RADIUS_RATIO
# Feature description: RADIUS_RATIO normalized by dividing it by PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO.
# Usefulness: Normalizing the RADIUS_RATIO by the primary axis aspect ratio provides insight into how the variety in radius compares to the proportional size of the vehicle. This can help differentiate geometries that belong to compact cars versus elongated vehicles such as buses and vans.
df['NORMALIZED_RADIUS_RATIO'] = df['RADIUS_RATIO'] / (df['PR.AXIS_ASPECT_RATIO'] + 1e-5)
end

